    "note": "John 21:23 itself says Jesus did not say John would not die; the Gospel writer corrects exactly this rumour. Early tradition (Irenaeus, Polycrates of Ephesus) records John dying of old age in Ephesus around AD 100, with a tomb there; the boiling‑oil story is a later legend (Tertullian). Scripture teaches that all people die until Christ returns. Charitable reading: John’s long life and survival of persecution are well attested, and the preacher may be stressing life in Christ rather than literal deathlessness.",
