    "note": "ʾāḥôr means “back” and, temporally, more often “afterward” than “past.” In Exod 33–34 God answers the request for glory by proclaiming His goodness and name (merciful, gracious, abounding in love). Scripture does call humans God’s image and glory (1 Cor 11:7; Ps 8:5), and Christ the radiance of His glory (Heb 1:3), but most theology distinguishes God’s own glory from the creatures who reflect it (Isa 42:8). Reading the rock as Christ has a long typological history.",
